From: Sébastien Taylor <sebastien@au-zone.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] staging: neutron: import DMA_BUF namespace

The driver now calls dma_buf_export(), dma_buf_get(), dma_buf_put() and
dma_buf_fd(), which are exported in the DMA_BUF symbol namespace.  Kernels
that build neutron as a module (CONFIG_NEUTRON=m) fail modpost without the
import; built-in kernels do not run that check.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded platform specific]
Signed-off-by: Sébastien Taylor <sebastien@au-zone.com>
---
 drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_buffer.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_buffer.c
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@
 #include "neutron_device.h"
 #include "uapi/neutron.h"
 
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS(DMA_BUF);
+
 /****************************************************************************/
 
 static void neutron_buffer_destroy(struct kref *kref)
-- 
2.43.0
